      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you, and the pain you're feeling is incredibly valid. Feeling like you need to step away to survive is a natural response in the face of overwhelming adversity. Sometimes, to heal, we focus on self-care and finding a safe haven for ourselves, where we don't have to confront the dysfunctional systems. Please remember that it's okay to take a step back to ensure your well-being doesn't deteriorate further. You don't have to go through this alone, even if it seems like you are. In time, you may find a different way for yourself to cope and maybe even a new place where your struggles won't hinder others. If you change your mind about reaching out, I'm here for you. But if you're serious about stepping away, there's no harm in giving yourself permission to do so while you grieve. Your feelings and your mental health are the most important things right now. If you really want it, I can help you find resources to make that process as smooth as possible.",
